# ---- motor_ai_sim API environment - TEMPLATE -------------------------------
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   The OAuth client id used to be written straight into scripts/start_api.cmd
#   and committed (migration plan section 3, "the OAuth client id is currently
#   committed in a repo file").  A client id is not a password - the browser
#   sends it in the clear - but a value that lives in git is a value nobody can
#   rotate without a commit, and the same .cmd is where a real secret
#   (AUTH_SECRET, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) would be typed next.  So: the .cmd reads
#   this file, and the real one is gitignored.
#
# FORMAT: plain KEY=value, ASCII, one per line, NO quotes and NO trailing
# spaces (both become part of the value).  `#` starts a comment line.
# Deliberately the SAME format on both sides:
#
#   Windows workstation   scripts\api.env         parsed by start_api.cmd
#   Linux server          /etc/motres/api.env     root:root 0600, loaded by
#                         docker-compose `env_file` or systemd
#                         `EnvironmentFile` - see deploy/README.md
#
# so a value proven on one is the value that ships on the other.
#
# HOW TO USE (this Windows workstation)
#   copy scripts\api.env.example scripts\api.env
#   ...fill in the values...
#   cmd /c scripts\start_api.cmd --print-env      (proves it is read)
#   schtasks /run /tn motor_ai_sim_api

# Google sign-in (docs/GOOGLE_SIGNIN_SETUP.md).  Must equal the frontend's
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID.  Empty = Google sign-in off.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# 1 = real enforcement (anonymous callers get tier "anon").
AUTH_ENFORCE=1

# Comma-separated e-mails that are ALWAYS admin.
ADMIN_EMAILS=vadim@motresres.com

# HS256 session-signing secret.  Empty on this workstation = generated into
# config\.auth_secret on first use.  ON THE SERVER SET IT EXPLICITLY: a lost
# .auth_secret signs every account out permanently and users.py deliberately
# refuses to mint a replacement.   openssl rand -hex 32
AUTH_SECRET=

# In-app AI support assistant.  Empty = /api/support/chat serves a flagged
# mock reply instead of calling out.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---- server only (the four roots + the queue) -------------------------------
# Unset on the workstation: with WORKSPACES_ROOT unset the whole multi-user
# layer is off and every path is the process config directory, exactly as it
# was before the migration.  Set ALL FOUR together on the server.
#
# The three layers of the read-through catalog (migration plan section 2.1).
# SHARED_ROOT is mounted READ-ONLY in the container.
# WORKSPACES_ROOT=/srv/motres/workspaces
# PUBLISHED_ROOT=/srv/motres/published
# SHARED_ROOT=/srv/motres/shared
#
# THE IDENTITY TRAP.  users.json, .auth_secret and .sessions.json resolve from
# the folder of MOTOR_AI_SIM_CONFIG - they are NOT workspace-scoped and never
# should be.  Pointing the process config at /srv/motres/identity is what puts
# the identity layer where the backup set expects it.
# MOTOR_AI_SIM_CONFIG=/srv/motres/identity/motor_config.yaml
#
# Solver workers = physical cores / 4 (migration plan section 2.4).  2 on an
# AX42 (8 c / 16 t), 4 on an AX102.  Measured: a pool of 10 pinned workers
# stretched a 60 s eval to a 231 s median.
# QUEUE_WORKERS=2
#
# Extra CORS origins, comma-separated.  Only needed if the frontend is served
# from a DIFFERENT origin than the API; the same-origin nginx default is not.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://emotres.com
